::  name       tablecloth content budget
::  shape      content-bytes -- int (@u32), bound 512
::  invariant  one artifact's whole content fits what a single bead-index can address
::  example    512
::  readers    Tablecloth - Mantra beading - Glow Tend - shape museum
::  nib        tablecloth-v1 at 20260812.142132
::
::  Tablecloth's second pedestal, and the first in this room whose number its own module never
::  spells. brushstroke/tablecloth.rye declares the bound as
::  `pub const max_content_bytes: u32 = beading.max_resin_bytes;` -- a derivation, so the value
::  is decided one room over, in mantra/beading.rye, where `max_resin_bytes` reads 512. Walk to
::  the declaring file and you find a name; the deciding file holds the number. So this desk
::  cites both rooms, and the guard beside it reads 512 out of beading rather than out of itself.
::
::  Why the derivation is its own reading. Respell tablecloth's line as a literal 512 and every
::  number here still agrees, while the sentence above has quietly become false: the artifact
::  budget would no longer follow the resin budget, and the next honest raise of
::  `max_resin_bytes` would leave the two apart with nothing to say so. So the guard reads the
::  derivation as a fact of its own, beside the values it compares.
+$  tablecloth-content-budget-shape
  $:  content-bytes=@u32
  ==
